# Build context allowlist for `docker build .` at this repo root.
#
# DENY EVERYTHING, then re-admit only what a Dockerfile in this repo actually
# needs. This is an allowlist on purpose, for two reasons that are not stylistic:
#
# 1. SIZE. The repo root holds ~12 GB of checkpoint shards and a ~6 GB .venv. A
#    default (empty) context would ship all of it to the Docker daemon on every
#    build, for a Dockerfile whose only COPY is three Python files.
#
# 2. SECRETS. `.env` lives at this repo root. With a permissive context it sits
#    inside every build, one careless `COPY . .` away from being baked into a
#    layer — while docker/lerobot-policy/Dockerfile goes to real trouble to pass
#    HF_TOKEN as a BuildKit `--secret` precisely so it never persists. An
#    allowlist makes that leak structurally impossible rather than merely
#    unlikely.
#
# Adding a new COPY to a Dockerfile therefore requires adding its path here. That
# is the intended friction: it forces the decision to be explicit.
*

!docker/lerobot-policy/

# Admitted by plan 06-03, which added `COPY policy_guard/ /app/policy_guard/` to
# docker/lerobot-policy/Dockerfile so the SAFE-01 guard has ONE implementation
# across the process boundary instead of a second copy inside the image. This
# entry is the explicit decision the header above demands: it admits ~20 KB of
# first-party Python (two files, one of them 0 bytes) and no secret — `.env`
# stays denied by the `*` above, and `policy_guard/` holds no credential, no
# checkpoint and no build artifact.
!policy_guard/

# Normal serving uses the shared lightweight observer; admit only its launcher.
!scripts/
scripts/*
!scripts/serve_observed_lerobot.py
!scripts/serve_observed_native.py
!scripts/replay_groot_native.py

# Evaluation-only model server: no credentials, checkpoints or user outputs.
!docker/model-swap/
!policy_lab/
policy_lab/**/__pycache__/
policy_lab/**/*.pyc
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
